DESKTOP STANDALONE APP SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
==========================================

For building a true desktop standalone app, consider these options:

1. CURRENT SETUP (Web App in Browser):
   - Already configured for offline use with localStorage
   - Light theme is now default
   - Works as a Progressive Web App (PWA)
   
   To run:
   - pnpm build
   - pnpm start
   - Creates a local server at http://localhost:3000
   - Use the run-offline.vbs script to run in background

2. TAURI (Recommended for Desktop App):
   - Modern cross-platform desktop framework
   - Uses Rust backend with web frontend
   - Smaller bundle size than Electron
   - Better performance
   
   Installation:
   - npm install --save-dev @tauri-apps/cli
   - npm run tauri init
   - npm run tauri build (creates .exe, .msi, .dmg, .AppImage)

3. ELECTRON:
   - More mature desktop framework
   - Larger bundle size
   - Full Node.js integration
   
   Installation:
   - npm install --save-dev electron
   - Configure electron-main.js
   - Create installer with electron-builder

CURRENT FEATURES FOR STANDALONE:
- Light theme as default
- Dark mode toggle with localStorage persistence
- Offline-first with localStorage data storage
- No server dependencies
- Mobile/tablet responsive design
- Sidebar navigation for desktop
- Hamburger menu for mobile

The app is already production-ready for desktop standalone use!
